--[[
        R E D   S E E K

        Paints the Seek chase red and watches whether you live through it.

        Loaded once per run by MainScript. Handles two models:

            SeekMovingNewClone   the chase Seek. Surviving one awards
                                 "You Survived Red Seek".
            Eye                  painted as well, no achievement of its own.

        NOTE ON STRIPTEXTURES
        ---------------------
        A part wearing a SurfaceAppearance, or a MeshPart with a TextureID,
        draws its texture and ignores Color entirely. Setting the colour on
        those does nothing you can see. StripTextures removes them so the red
        actually shows.

        It only touches the local clone of the chase model, which is thrown
        away when the chase ends, so nothing permanent is damaged. Turn it off
        if you would rather keep Seek's textures and accept a weaker tint.
]]

local Core = loadstring(game:HttpGet(
	"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bonellocristian78-lab/Gradish-Mode/main/GradishCore"
))()

Core.RedSeek:Enable({
	Color = Color3.fromRGB(255, 0, 0),

	-- Models to paint. Add any other name you want turned red.
	Models = { "SeekMovingNewClone", "Eye" },

	-- Which of those counts as the chase for the achievement.
	SeekName = "SeekMovingNewClone",

	-- See the note above. Without this most of Seek stays its normal colour.
	StripTextures = true,

	-- How long to wait after the model disappears before deciding you
	-- survived. The model is removed whether you escaped or were caught, and
	-- on a catch the removal can land a frame before your health hits zero.
	DeathGrace = 1.5,

	-- How often to sweep for a model that appeared nested somewhere instead of
	-- directly under Workspace.
	PollInterval = 2,
})
